s first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal erythrocyte morphology, bleeding gums, blurred vision, bone pain\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Essential Thrombocythemia (ET):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, ascites\n  Favours second: abnormal cerebral vascular morphology, abnormal platelet morphology, abnormal thrombocyte morphology, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology, amaurosis fugax\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Primary Myelofibrosis (PMF):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, ascites\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal megakaryocyte morphology, abnormal thrombosis, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Multiple Myeloma (Plasma Cell Neoplasm):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: anemia, bone pain, constipation, frequent urination, hyperviscosity syndrome"}
